@include ../../shared/squash.overtone

## Backhand ladder volleys
Backhand ladder volleys, five minutes. Start within two metres of the front wall, on your backhand
side, a metre or so off the side wall: soft volleys above the service line, hitting each one again
before it bounces. Then move back behind the tape for your volley ladder level: halfway to the
short line, three-quarters of the way, or the short line itself. Let it bounce if you lose it.
Phase two target: twenty without a break from the three-quarter line.
+0:00.5 [countdown]
--- 5:00
0:00 [go]
7% Racket high. Punch, then extend up.
20% Firm wrist.
33% Move back to your ladder line. Serve it up, and keep volleying.
45% Racket high. Punch.
58% Count them. Lose it? Restart, and count from zero.
72% Shoulders to the side wall.
85% Last minute. Your best run of the day.
-0:10 Ten seconds.
---
[stop]
